  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In dehydrohalogenation reactions,&nbsp;the preferred product is that alkene which has the greater number of alkyl groups attached to the doubly bonded carbon atoms. Thus, 2-bromopentane gives pent-2-ene as the major product.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0062_8eb19b29d802.png\" style=\"width: 446px; height: 103px;\" />Rest all bromides are having only one type of beta hydrogen, hence, only one possible alkene is formed.</p>"
